        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6ac70633-e681-5294-8a03-6b2b8b83292b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Moominpappa at Sea, The Old Man and the Sea, Moominvalley in November, Who Will Comfort Toffle?\n- People: Ernest Hemingway, Tove Jansson\n- Topics: Moomin series, literary references, publication chronology\n\nFacts:\n- The Old Man and the Sea is a short novel by Ernest Hemingway that he wrote in 1951 in Bimini, Bahamas, and published in 1952.\n- Moominpappa at Sea has an original title that loosely references Ernest Hemingway's novel The Old Man and the Sea, but that reference is not preserved in translation.\n- Moominpappa at Sea was published in 1965.\n- Moominvalley in November is set contemporaneously with Moominpappa at Sea (1965).\n- Moominvalley in November is the only installment in the series in which the Moomin family are absent.\n- Who Will Comfort Toffle? is the second picture book in the Moomin series by Tove Jansson.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
