        "text": "Page: Moominpappa at Sea. Sentence: The original title is a loose reference to Hemingway novel \"The Old Man and the Sea\", though this is not reflected in the translation.\nPage: The Old Man and the Sea. Sentence: The Old Man and the Sea is a short novel written by the American author Ernest Hemingway in 1951 in Bimini, Bahamas, and published in 1952.\nPage: Moominvalley in November. Sentence: Set contemporaneously with her previous novel \"Moominpappa at Sea\" (1965), it is the only installment in the series where the titular Moomin family are actually absent.\nPage: Who Will Comfort Toffle?. Sentence: is the second picture book in the Moomin series by Tove Jansson.",
